+
+| Term | Definition |
+|---|---|
+| [+voiced] | words that leave a mouth as sound: the quoted words of any message (`quotes.ts`; SillyTavern sets them in `<q>`) |
+| [−voiced] | every other stretch of text: an account of the scene or of an act, or words formed without sound |
+| unit | a stretch of a paragraph with one value of [±voiced]; a block that is no paragraph (a block quotation, a list, a table) is one unit |
+
+| IF | THEN |
+|---|---|
+| a paragraph has quoted parts | each quoted part is a unit, and the parts between two of them are one unit |
+| a stretch between two units has no letter or digit (", " or ".") | it joins the unit before it; at the paragraph's start, the one after it |
+| the unit shown is [+voiced] | its text is the ink (black) and the plate says "speaking" |
+| the unit shown is [−voiced] | its text is darkslateblue (8.99:1 on ivory) and the plate says no "speaking"; "thinking" stays where a WorkOut call put it |
+| a tap on the text, → or › | the next unit; after a message's last unit, the next message's first |
+| ← or ‹ | the unit before; before a message's first unit, the last of the message before |
+| "Log" | the whole chat, scrolling, with the same colours and without pictures; "Box" returns |
+| a message is being written or edited, or the setting "a box holds a whole message" | the message shows whole in the box |
+| a message is drawn anew (the player's line, a reply) | the box goes to its first unit |
+
+The speaker named on the plate is the message's author. Inside a narrator's message the one who says a quoted part is not known to the engine, so the plate says "speaking" beside the narrator's name. The box keeps four lines' height and scrolls past 60 % of the screen's height [ASSUMED: both]. The bar's buttons are 44 px or more each way (WCAG 2.5.5).
